1
00:00:05,130 --> 00:00:06,640
Miyata Akihiro...

2
00:00:08,380 --> 00:00:11,000
Will you be my partner
for the rest of our lives?

3
00:00:25,190 --> 00:00:26,390
I'm sorry!

4
00:00:34,820 --> 00:00:36,630
I can't answer you right now.

5
00:00:39,646 --> 00:00:41,390
Can you tell me why?

6
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:45,500
Did I...

7
00:00:47,750 --> 00:00:49,600
do something wrong?

8
00:00:55,090 --> 00:00:56,610
It's not you.

9
00:00:57,550 --> 00:00:58,990
It's me.

10
00:01:11,690 --> 00:01:14,030
My mind is a complete mess right now.

11
00:01:18,780 --> 00:01:20,030
What do you mean?

12
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:26,470
Your new book might fall through.

13
00:01:33,260 --> 00:01:34,860
Masumoto-san, the consultant, said

14
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:38,690
they want to rework the whole book
with Business Bear as the lead.

15
00:01:40,850 --> 00:01:43,780
She'll probably contact you directly soon.

16
00:01:48,100 --> 00:01:49,510
As your editor,

17
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:52,830
I feel so useless
for failing to protect your book.

18
00:01:53,860 --> 00:01:56,420
Right now, that's all I can think about.

19
00:01:58,740 --> 00:02:00,630
I picked the wrong time, didn't I?

20
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:03,080
I'm sorry.

21
00:02:06,410 --> 00:02:07,720
I might...

22
00:02:09,460 --> 00:02:12,440
quit the company
and become a freelance editor...

23
00:02:13,420 --> 00:02:15,510
If that happens,
I'll support you no matter what.

24
00:02:15,550 --> 00:02:16,880
You don't need to worry about money??

25
00:02:16,900 --> 00:02:18,320
Please don't do that.

26
00:02:22,680 --> 00:02:24,120
When it comes to my living expenses,

27
00:02:25,140 --> 00:02:26,870
I want to earn my own way.

28
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:33,020
Maybe that's just
my foolish pride talking.

29
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:40,510
No...

30
00:02:42,410 --> 00:02:43,510
It's all right.

31
00:02:46,950 --> 00:02:47,960
So...

32
00:02:49,160 --> 00:02:51,020
until all of this is sorted out,

33
00:02:51,750 --> 00:02:53,540
could you please wait for my answer?

34
00:03:14,820 --> 00:03:16,330
The two of us...

35
00:03:16,530 --> 00:03:18,880
Maybe we've both grown too mature.

36
00:03:22,780 --> 00:03:24,760
Over these past two years...

37
00:03:31,540 --> 00:03:34,410
I thought the distance between us
had finally closed to nothing.

38
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:41,050
Good night.

39
00:03:44,090 --> 00:03:45,200
Good night.

40
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:55,960
To think I believed it so blindly...

41
00:03:56,150 --> 00:03:57,500
I was the fool all along.

42
00:04:02,570 --> 00:04:03,570
Because right now,

43
00:04:03,820 --> 00:04:05,470
you feel so far away.

44
00:04:18,400 --> 00:04:23,000
"Love is Better the Second Time Around season2"
(Episode 6)

45
00:05:08,780 --> 00:05:09,880
Takashi.

46
00:05:17,020 --> 00:05:18,120
Long time no see.

47
00:05:19,860 --> 00:05:20,960
Sota.

48
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:28,120
You haven't changed a bit.

49
00:05:28,660 --> 00:05:29,660
Neither have you.

50
00:05:29,990 --> 00:05:30,990
You think so?

51
00:05:31,490 --> 00:05:34,430
As you can see,
I'm practically buried in books.

52
00:05:35,040 --> 00:05:37,640
We're just a tiny publishing house
run by three people, after all.

53
00:05:38,080 --> 00:05:41,130
My staff keeps telling me
I should be more business-minded.

54
00:05:41,750 --> 00:05:44,460
Still doing what you love,
just like always.

55
00:05:45,300 --> 00:05:46,550
In this day and age?

56
00:05:46,590 --> 00:05:47,990
I must look like an idiot.

57
00:05:48,220 --> 00:05:52,680
Not at all. I think it's
wonderful. It's so like you.

58
00:05:58,190 --> 00:05:59,270
I know how busy you are,

59
00:05:59,770 --> 00:06:01,970
so thanks for making time to meet.

60
00:06:02,650 --> 00:06:03,900
Don't mention it.

61
00:06:04,780 --> 00:06:06,450
I was really happy to hear from you.

62
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:09,200
Me too.

63
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:11,550
It's great to see you again.

64
00:06:21,380 --> 00:06:22,890
No worries.

65
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:31,389
Um...

66
00:06:31,390 --> 00:06:32,550
Miyata.

67
00:06:33,010 --> 00:06:34,010
Yes?

68
00:06:34,640 --> 00:06:37,370
About Teacher Iwanaga's book...

69
00:06:39,690 --> 00:06:42,120
Still no go?

70
00:06:42,810 --> 00:06:43,820
Yeah.

71
00:06:45,440 --> 00:06:47,920
Looks like they're going with
Masumoto-san's proposal.

72
00:06:50,070 --> 00:06:51,070
I see...

73
00:06:55,290 --> 00:06:56,830
All right!

74
00:06:58,790 --> 00:06:59,790
Let's call it a day.

75
00:07:01,170 --> 00:07:02,390
- Okay.
- Yeah.

76
00:07:04,290 --> 00:07:05,300
Let's head out.

77
00:07:07,590 --> 00:07:10,510
I keep talking about
striking out on my own,

78
00:07:10,760 --> 00:07:13,510
but with my kid taking
middle school entrance exams,

79
00:07:13,650 --> 00:07:15,390
money is really tight.

80
00:07:16,060 --> 00:07:19,140
Who knows how much longer
this industry will last, anyway.

81
00:07:22,350 --> 00:07:25,570
I miss the days
when books practically sold themselves.

82
00:07:25,650 --> 00:07:26,350
Yeah.

83
00:07:26,351 --> 00:07:28,570
Thank you for waiting.
Here is the crab cream croquette.

84
00:07:28,610 --> 00:07:29,320
Oh.

85
00:07:29,321 --> 00:07:31,950
I didn't order this.
It must be for these gentlemen.

86
00:07:31,990 --> 00:07:32,990
I'm so sorry!

87
00:07:33,590 --> 00:07:34,649
Here is your crab cream croquette.

88
00:07:34,650 --> 00:07:36,070
- Oh, thanks!
- Thank you.

89
00:07:36,200 --> 00:07:37,200
Enjoy!

90
00:07:37,740 --> 00:07:38,450
Thanks.

91
00:07:38,451 --> 00:07:41,830
Excuse me, I couldn't help overhearing...

92
00:07:42,080 --> 00:07:43,680
Are you two in publishing as well?

93
00:07:44,450 --> 00:07:46,040
Yeah, we are.

94
00:07:46,670 --> 00:07:47,840
I work in publishing too.

95
00:07:48,050 --> 00:07:49,210
Oh, really?

96
00:07:49,300 --> 00:07:50,550
A fellow publisher!

97
00:07:53,750 --> 00:07:54,750
What a small world.

98
00:07:55,140 --> 00:07:56,509
- Here.
- Cheers!

99
00:07:56,510 --> 00:07:57,970
Cheers!

100
00:08:01,060 --> 00:08:06,270
Everything cultural has
become so disposable these days.

101
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:09,109
I just can't keep up with that pace.

102
00:08:09,110 --> 00:08:11,206
No yeah, I completely understand.

103
00:08:12,240 --> 00:08:17,409
Our company doesn't chase bestsellers
either. We want to walk alongside our authors

104
00:08:17,410 --> 00:08:20,950
and pour our hearts
into crafting every book.

105
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:23,430
Our hope is for readers

106
00:08:23,580 --> 00:08:26,750
to fall deeply in love with each title
and become true lifelong fans.

107
00:08:29,920 --> 00:08:31,799
Wow, that's nothing like our company.

108
00:08:31,800 --> 00:08:35,149
Well, we're small.
We wouldn't survive any other way.

109
00:08:35,150 --> 00:08:37,680
Even so, it's truly admirable.

110
00:08:37,710 --> 00:08:39,269
Here are three ice waters.
Thank you for waiting.

111
00:08:39,270 --> 00:08:39,970
Thanks.

112
00:08:39,970 --> 00:08:40,970
Thank you.

113
00:08:42,430 --> 00:08:43,440
Take your time.

114
00:08:47,860 --> 00:08:49,110
Miyata.

115
00:08:49,530 --> 00:08:50,630
Drink some water.

116
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:52,610
Thank you.

117
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:55,200
Hasegawa-san, have some too.

118
00:08:55,570 --> 00:08:56,570
Thanks.

119
00:09:07,500 --> 00:09:10,936
Just having someone so wonderful by your side
is something to be grateful for, isn't it?

120
00:09:10,960 --> 00:09:13,300
You couldn't be more right!

121
00:09:16,220 --> 00:09:17,690
What about you, Arima-san?

122
00:09:18,140 --> 00:09:20,100
Don't you have someone special?

123
00:09:24,600 --> 00:09:26,620
I did, back in college.

124
00:09:26,650 --> 00:09:27,650
Though,

125
00:09:27,770 --> 00:09:29,820
after we split, nothing really worked out.

126
00:09:31,110 --> 00:09:32,110
Did you get dumped?

127
00:09:33,150 --> 00:09:34,150
No.

128
00:09:34,320 --> 00:09:35,900
I ended it myself.

129
00:09:36,530 --> 00:09:38,330
He was amazing right up until the end.

130
00:09:38,660 --> 00:09:39,680
Oh?

131
00:09:39,990 --> 00:09:41,830
Then why did you dump him?

132
00:09:42,620 --> 00:09:43,870
Well... it's a long story.

133
00:09:44,160 --> 00:09:45,790
I see.

134
00:09:48,710 --> 00:09:50,170
Actually,

135
00:09:50,790 --> 00:09:52,300
I've been in the same boat.

136
00:09:53,960 --> 00:09:59,070
My partner and I broke up once before, too.

137
00:09:59,930 --> 00:10:02,530
But when we crossed paths
again, we got back together.

138
00:10:02,930 --> 00:10:04,810
Miyata, I had no idea
you were such a romantic.

139
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:08,520
So you could do the same, Arima-san.

140
00:10:09,100 --> 00:10:11,330
If you still have feelings for him,

141
00:10:12,020 --> 00:10:14,540
why not just start over now?

142
00:10:17,360 --> 00:10:18,360
Thank you.

143
00:10:19,620 --> 00:10:20,820
Actually, just recently,

144
00:10:21,330 --> 00:10:23,220
he reached out to me.

145
00:10:24,290 --> 00:10:25,449
Maybe this will be our turning point.

146
00:10:25,450 --> 00:10:27,540
That's great!

147
00:10:28,870 --> 00:10:29,880
Yeah.

148
00:10:34,950 --> 00:10:36,830
- Here you go.
- Thanks.

149
00:10:40,550 --> 00:10:43,570
Let's dive right in.
Please take a look at this.

150
00:10:44,810 --> 00:10:46,600
Here is the new cover proposal.

151
00:10:47,520 --> 00:10:50,650
By featuring Business Bear
prominently on the cover,

152
00:10:50,690 --> 00:10:54,320
we think we can reach a wider readership.

153
00:10:54,480 --> 00:10:56,610
The concept certainly
has commercial appeal.

154
00:10:57,740 --> 00:11:01,260
As expected of Teacher Iwanaga.
You caught on right away.

155
00:11:02,740 --> 00:11:04,760
- Well then...
- I refuse.

156
00:11:10,620 --> 00:11:12,180
May I ask why?

157
00:11:13,710 --> 00:11:16,710
Miyata and I poured
everything into this book.

158
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:19,840
I will never accept turning it
into something completely different.

159
00:11:20,220 --> 00:11:21,720
Be that as it may...

160
00:11:22,050 --> 00:11:24,110
I am officially terminating our contract.

161
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:33,250
I thought Tokyo Commercial Publishing and I
had built a solid partnership.

162
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:36,230
It's deeply regrettable.

163
00:11:38,940 --> 00:11:42,450
I am so sorry.

164
00:11:45,620 --> 00:11:47,430
A real shame.

165
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:54,180
Now, I'd like to speak
with Miyata in private.

166
00:11:57,340 --> 00:11:58,860
Then we'll take our leave.

167
00:12:07,260 --> 00:12:08,660
I startled you, didn't I?

168
00:12:11,020 --> 00:12:13,080
You really didn't have to go that far...

169
00:12:15,020 --> 00:12:17,790
What will happen to our book now?

170
00:12:19,530 --> 00:12:21,090
There's still hope.

171
00:12:22,030 --> 00:12:23,030
What?

172
00:12:23,320 --> 00:12:25,200
Once the contract is canceled,

173
00:12:25,490 --> 00:12:27,700
the publisher forfeits
the publishing rights,

174
00:12:28,120 --> 00:12:30,350
while the copyright
remains with the author.

175
00:12:30,790 --> 00:12:32,159
In other words,

176
00:12:32,160 --> 00:12:35,210
I can publish this book
through someone else.

177
00:12:36,500 --> 00:12:38,500
Where would we even
find a publisher willing to...

178
00:12:39,630 --> 00:12:41,060
I've already lined one up.

179
00:12:41,840 --> 00:12:43,730
Someone I trust completely.

180
00:12:45,390 --> 00:12:48,140
But I won't be able to be involved...

181
00:12:51,060 --> 00:12:53,040
Unless you go freelance.

182
00:12:57,731 --> 00:13:01,751
[A blog post about how someone quit their
corporate job and became a freelancer]

183
00:13:26,050 --> 00:13:27,050
Um...

184
00:13:28,640 --> 00:13:29,640
Tonight...

185
00:13:31,100 --> 00:13:32,100
Can't we?

186
00:13:35,560 --> 00:13:37,190
I'm a little tired.

187
00:13:39,730 --> 00:13:40,940
I see.

188
00:13:42,280 --> 00:13:43,400
Next time, okay?

189
00:13:44,860 --> 00:13:45,860
Yeah.

190
00:13:49,950 --> 00:13:51,700
We need to fix that cut,

191
00:13:53,160 --> 00:13:56,120
and make sure Business Bear
and the professor are separated.

192
00:13:56,790 --> 00:13:58,880
Stagger them clearly
to balance the left side.

193
00:13:59,370 --> 00:14:01,750
I'll try that in the edit.

194
00:14:03,410 --> 00:14:04,969
I'll leave it to you, then.

195
00:14:04,970 --> 00:14:06,009
I'll send it over once it's done.

196
00:14:06,010 --> 00:14:07,010
Got it.

197
00:14:21,820 --> 00:14:24,400
He doesn't have an ounce of deceit in him.

198
00:14:25,070 --> 00:14:27,090
Quite the opposite of me.

199
00:14:27,320 --> 00:14:28,660
What are you talking about?

200
00:14:28,740 --> 00:14:30,500
You're definitely going
to like him, Miyata.

201
00:14:35,790 --> 00:14:36,790
Oh.

202
00:14:38,370 --> 00:14:40,210
Let me introduce you. This is??

203
00:14:42,250 --> 00:14:43,419
Arima-san?!

204
00:14:43,420 --> 00:14:45,210
Wait, Miyata?!

205
00:14:45,380 --> 00:14:45,960
Huh?

206
00:14:46,050 --> 00:14:47,340
You two know each other?

207
00:14:47,720 --> 00:14:50,930
We sat next to each other at an izakaya
the other night and totally hit it off.

208
00:14:50,950 --> 00:14:52,550
- What a surprise!
- Seriously!

209
00:14:55,100 --> 00:14:56,100
Have a seat.

210
00:14:57,020 --> 00:14:59,520
I had no idea you'd
already met Miyata, Sota.

211
00:15:00,480 --> 00:15:01,810
That makes things so much easier.

212
00:15:02,400 --> 00:15:03,690
If it's Arima-san,

213
00:15:03,820 --> 00:15:05,820
I know the book will be in great hands.

214
00:15:06,190 --> 00:15:07,440
Thank you.

215
00:15:07,610 --> 00:15:08,610
The pleasure's mine.

216
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:11,950
Still, when Takashi told me,

217
00:15:11,990 --> 00:15:14,030
I thought he was being way too reckless.

218
00:15:14,990 --> 00:15:15,840
Yeah.

219
00:15:15,950 --> 00:15:17,999
Then again, it's classic you.

220
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,269
Hm? What's that supposed to mean?

221
00:15:20,270 --> 00:15:22,270
Remember back in our junior year?

222
00:15:25,300 --> 00:15:27,919
Were you two classmates in college?

223
00:15:27,920 --> 00:15:28,920
Yeah.

224
00:15:28,987 --> 00:15:32,116
Takashi got into a huge fight
with the upperclassmen in the debate club,

225
00:15:32,140 --> 00:15:34,560
and then went ahead and
started his own club, didn't you?

226
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:35,930
You make it sound terrible.

227
00:15:36,520 --> 00:15:38,020
It was just an academic disagreement.

228
00:15:38,030 --> 00:15:40,770
And then at the very next tournament,

229
00:15:41,150 --> 00:15:43,230
he completely crushed those seniors.

230
00:15:44,480 --> 00:15:45,870
Showed zero mercy.

231
00:15:45,980 --> 00:15:48,570
I wish you wouldn't bring that up.

232
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:50,240
Still,

233
00:15:50,820 --> 00:15:52,340
that's just who he is.

234
00:15:52,360 --> 00:15:53,880
So I wasn't all that surprised.

235
00:16:09,630 --> 00:16:12,720
Who gave you this watch?

236
00:16:13,590 --> 00:16:15,890
Someone I was close to in college.

237
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:19,810
You've been wearing
that watch a lot lately.

238
00:16:19,890 --> 00:16:22,330
My other one broke.

239
00:16:31,740 --> 00:16:32,740
Actually, just recently,

240
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:35,260
he reached out to me.

241
00:16:36,160 --> 00:16:37,409
Maybe this will be our turning point.

242
00:16:37,410 --> 00:16:39,830
That's great!

243
00:16:43,250 --> 00:16:45,020
Should we get down to discussing the book?

244
00:16:45,170 --> 00:16:46,410
Right, of course. My apologies.

245
00:16:47,460 --> 00:16:49,800
I've already filled Sota in on the basics,

246
00:16:50,210 --> 00:16:53,250
but before we sign anything, is there
anything you'd like to ask him, Miyata?

247
00:16:56,260 --> 00:16:57,400
Miyata?

248
00:16:59,770 --> 00:17:00,770
I'm sorry.

249
00:17:01,640 --> 00:17:03,200
I'd like to reconsider this.

250
00:17:03,730 --> 00:17:04,730
Please excuse me.

251
00:17:13,950 --> 00:17:15,050
Miyata!

252
00:17:48,270 --> 00:17:49,790
Takashi, is he...

253
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:03,700
He's that guy, isn't he?

254
00:18:56,800 --> 00:18:57,800
Miyata...!

255
00:19:09,230 --> 00:19:10,440
Miyata?

256
00:19:19,200 --> 00:19:20,710
Did you two date?

257
00:19:23,370 --> 00:19:24,620
You and Arima-san...

258
00:19:27,660 --> 00:19:28,660
Yeah...

259
00:19:30,710 --> 00:19:31,890
I knew it.

260
00:19:36,710 --> 00:19:39,070
He really is an amazing person.

261
00:19:40,130 --> 00:19:43,360
He barely knows us,
yet he's willing to help out.

262
00:19:46,600 --> 00:19:48,600
The vibe between you and Arima-san...

263
00:19:49,520 --> 00:19:53,560
It's like nothing I've ever seen before.
You look great together.

264
00:19:55,110 --> 00:19:57,130
We're just friends.

265
00:19:57,820 --> 00:20:00,360
And besides, he dumped me, so...

266
00:20:00,361 --> 00:20:02,320
Maybe you could have a second chance, too.

267
00:20:03,530 --> 00:20:05,240
Just like we did.

268
00:20:18,510 --> 00:20:19,650
Sota...

269
00:20:21,260 --> 00:20:24,220
pulled me out when I hit rock bottom.

270
00:20:26,850 --> 00:20:28,970
Even though I'm choosing
a future with you now,

271
00:20:31,060 --> 00:20:34,080
that doesn't mean I can just erase my past.

272
00:20:39,650 --> 00:20:41,650
I'm sorry for saying something so foolish.

273
00:20:44,530 --> 00:20:49,393
When the truth is,
I've never once saved you.

274
00:20:53,960 --> 00:20:55,129
Miyata.

275
00:20:55,130 --> 00:20:56,130
That's not what I meant??

276
00:20:56,131 --> 00:20:57,811
Ever since I got back together with you...

277
00:20:58,550 --> 00:21:00,810
I've only hated myself more and more.

278
00:21:05,580 --> 00:21:06,580
I...

279
00:21:09,066 --> 00:21:12,086
I'll never know those sides
of you like your exes do,

280
00:21:12,480 --> 00:21:13,850
no matter what I do...

281
00:21:16,310 --> 00:21:18,370
I can't control how jealous I get.

282
00:21:27,950 --> 00:21:30,450
Turns out that's the kind of man I am.

283
00:21:34,710 --> 00:21:35,930
Jealous.

284
00:21:40,710 --> 00:21:42,260
Petty.

285
00:21:43,880 --> 00:21:46,010
A pathetic coward.

286
00:21:48,350 --> 00:21:50,240
I finally see myself for who I really am.

287
00:21:54,980 --> 00:21:56,870
Even you, Teacher Iwanaga,

288
00:21:57,520 --> 00:21:59,750
can't talk your way
out of this one, can you?

289
00:22:08,450 --> 00:22:10,510
You think that's how I see you?

290
00:22:19,880 --> 00:22:21,370
That's absurd!

291
00:22:23,050 --> 00:22:25,480
I love you with all my heart...

292
00:22:35,270 --> 00:22:37,010
Can't you bring yourself to believe in me?

293
00:22:44,190 --> 00:22:45,920
I don't think I can...

294
00:22:52,220 --> 00:22:54,300
Please forget about me.

295
00:22:59,080 --> 00:23:00,080
If you do...

296
00:23:02,340 --> 00:23:04,860
I think we'll both be
much happier in the end.

297
00:23:13,180 --> 00:23:14,520
There won't be...

298
00:23:16,810 --> 00:23:18,190
a third time for us.

299
00:23:34,800 --> 00:23:36,766
(Series Finale Preview)
(Where will their love lead?)

300
00:23:36,790 --> 00:23:37,999
You two broke up, didn't you?

301
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:40,919
Then I don't need to feel guilty anymore.

302
00:23:40,920 --> 00:23:44,570
Who do you think you are,
making Teacher Iwanaga cry?

303
00:23:44,600 --> 00:23:46,049
You bitch.

304
00:23:46,050 --> 00:23:47,320
My, my.

305
00:23:47,520 --> 00:23:48,990
You left me behind.

306
00:23:49,300 --> 00:23:50,230
Why?

307
00:23:50,231 --> 00:23:52,430
Because I didn't explain myself properly?

308
00:23:53,260 --> 00:23:54,349
Wait! Please wait!

309
00:23:54,350 --> 00:23:57,520
I'm not strong enough to go
through this again and again.

310
00:23:57,820 --> 00:23:59,690
If you had only told me back then...
